      ],
      "source": "https://www.brookfieldct.gov/165/History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s original name honored Reverend Thomas Brooks, the long‑time Congregational pastor after whom Brookfield was renamed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.brookfieldcthistory.org/home"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Brookfield once hosted a diverse industrial scene, including iron furnaces, grist mills, and a hat factory, reflecting its 18th‑century prosperity.",
